llvm-3.3 backport patch: a function's jump tables before its end label (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a function that holds a jump table
in its own section (every switch table under -fPIC on x86-64, which 3.3
prints as 32-bit label differences into the function's section): the
table is printed after the body and before the function's end label, so
that the function's symbol size and its unwind range (the .eh_frame FDE,
the source of config/functions.base.txt's sizes) cover the table, as the
PS4 compiler's library generation has it: the 54 in-text jump tables of
the library region (44 functions) all lie inside their function's FDE
range, and the first of them in a queue, FUN_000aa570, is the base's 64
bytes exactly (the code, one alignment nop, the table) with a symbol and
FDE that end at its last ret under the release 3.3. The 3.3 release prints
the tables after .size and .cfi_endproc (AsmPrinter::EmitFunctionBody),
as 3.6.2 and 4.0.0 do; 4.0.0 puts the tables in .rodata, which is what the
game region shows (497 tables, none in .text). docs/DECISIONS.md D28 holds
the measurement.

--- a/lib/CodeGen/AsmPrinter/AsmPrinter.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/AsmPrinter/AsmPrinter.cpp
@@ -757,6 +757,18 @@
   // Emit target-specific gunk after the function body.
   EmitFunctionBodyEnd();
 
+  // The PS4 compiler prints a function's jump tables before the function's
+  // end label, so that the function's size and its unwind range cover the
+  // tables it holds in its own section (docs/DECISIONS.md D28: 54 of 54
+  // in-text jump tables of the library region lie inside their function's
+  // FDE range). A table printed in another section leaves the current
+  // section as it was.
+  {
+    MCSectionSubPair FnSection = OutStreamer.getCurrentSection();
+    EmitJumpTableInfo();
+    OutStreamer.SwitchSection(FnSection.first, FnSection.second);
+  }
+
   // If the target wants a .size directive for the size of the function, emit
   // it.
   if (MAI->hasDotTypeDotSizeDirective()) {
@@ -784,9 +796,6 @@
   }
   MMI->EndFunction();
 
-  // Print out jump tables referenced by the function.
-  EmitJumpTableInfo();
-
   OutStreamer.AddBlankLine();
 }
 
